# ForgeTrail lessons gate (when + how)

This complements **`forgetrail-lessons-mcp.mdc`** (tool details + globs) and **`forgetrail-phase-status.mdc`** (phase footer).

## When to run the gate (do it early, before large edits)

Run **`getAntiPatterns`** once and **`searchLessons`** (one or more queries) when **any** of these is true:

- You expect to touch **≥3 files**, or **≥2** top-level areas (e.g. skill + site + docs).
- **New or changed** user-facing flow, skill contract, or site copy.
- The user asks for a **plan**, **feature**, **refactor**, or **milestone** that clearly spans multiple files.

**Skip the gate** for: single-file typos; renames with no behavior change; or when the user explicitly asks to skip.

## How to run it (order)

1. Call **`getAntiPatterns`** (no args). Skim for items that apply.
2. Call **`searchLessons`** with **2–4 short keyword queries**.
3. **Fold in before coding:** 3–6 bullets of what you will **do** or **avoid**. Do **not** paste full MCP dumps unless the user asks.

## Product-facing users

Do not mention MCP, tool names, or “lessons gate” in UI copy or user-facing summaries unless they ask how the workflow is wired up.
